The field mappings are handled both on the backend (to standardize data from Airtable) and on the frontend (to consume that standardized data). Here's a breakdown for the sections you've inquired about:

### Exhibitors

The `backend/src/routes/exhibitors.ts` file contains detailed logic for mapping various Airtable field names to the `Exhibitor` interface used by the frontend. The frontend (`app/exhibitors.tsx`) then consumes this standardized data.

**Frontend Interface (`app/exhibitors.tsx`):**

```typescript
interface Exhibitor {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  logo: string | null;
  description: string | null;
  contactName: string | null;
  contactTitle: string | null;
  contactEmail: string | null;
  contactPhoneDirect: string | null;
  contactPhoneMobile: string | null;
  contactFax: string | null;
  companyUrl: string | null;
  linkedIn: string | null;
  facebook: string | null;
  x: string | null;
  boothNumber: string | null;
  demonstrations: string | null;
}
```

**Key Backend Mappings (`backend/src/routes/exhibitors.ts`):**

The backend attempts to find data from several possible Airtable field names for flexibility:

*   **`id`**: Mapped directly from `record.id`.
*   **`name`**: Mapped from `record.fields.Name`.
*   **`description`**: Mapped from `record.fields.Description` or `record.fields.Bio`.
*   **`logoUrl` (becomes `logo` on frontend)**: Searched in Airtable fields like `Logo`, `Logo Url`, `Logo URL`, `LogoUrl`. It handles both attachment arrays (taking the first URL) and direct URL strings.
*   **`contactName`**: Searched in `Contact Name`, `Primary Contact Name`, `Primary contact name`, `Contact`, `Name (Contact)`.
*   **`contactTitle`**: Searched in `Contact Title`, `Primary Contact Title`, `Primary contact title`, `Title (Contact)`.
*   **`contactEmail`**: Searched in `Contact Email`, `Primary Contact Email`, `Primary contact email`, `Email`, `Email (Contact)`.
*   **`contactPhoneDirect` / `contactPhoneMobile`**: Searched in `Contact Phone`, `Primary Contact Phone`, `Primary contact phone`, `Phone`, `Direct Phone`, `Mobile Phone`. It distinguishes between direct and mobile based on the field name.
*   **`contactFax`**: Mapped from `Primary contact fax number` or `Contact Fax`.
*   **`companyUrl`**: Mapped from `URL`, `Company URL`, or `Website`.
*   **`linkedIn`**: Mapped from `record.fields.LinkedIn`.
*   **`facebook`**: Mapped from `Facebook URL`.
*   **`x`**: Mapped from `X (Twitter) URL`.
*   **`boothNumber`**: Mapped from `record.fields['Booth Number']` or `record.fields.BoothNumber`.
*   **`demonstrations`**: Mapped from `Demonstrations`.

### Sponsors

The frontend (`app/sponsors.tsx`) expects data that directly matches the `Sponsor` interface. The backend is responsible for providing this structure from the Airtable Sponsors/Partners table (`tblyI3hc2dZZu0eQA`).

**Frontend Interface (`app/sponsors.tsx`):**

```typescript
interface Sponsor {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  logo: string;
  tier: string;
  intro?: string;
  bio: string;
  website: string;
}
```

**Expected Airtable Field Mappings (from initial prompt and interface):**

*   **`id`**: Airtable record ID.
*   **`name`**: Sponsor's Name.
*   **`logo`**: URL of the sponsor's logo (likely from an attachment field).
*   **`tier`**: Sponsor's tier (e.g., "Platinum", "Gold").
*   **`intro`**: A short introduction.
*   **`bio`**: Full biography/description.
*   **`website`**: Sponsor's website URL.

### Announcements

Both the Home screen (`app/(tabs)/(home)/index.tsx`) and the Admin screen (`app/admin.tsx`) use the `Announcement` interface. The backend provides this data from the Airtable Announcements table (`tblGJQ3v4RMIXCP4W`).

**Frontend Interface (`app/(tabs)/(home)/index.tsx`, `app/admin.tsx`):**

```typescript
interface Announcement {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  content: string;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

**Expected Airtable Field Mappings (from initial prompt and interface):**

*   **`id`**: Airtable record ID.
*   **`title`**: Title of the announcement.
*   **`content`**: Full content of the announcement.
*   **`createdAt`**: Timestamp when the announcement was created.

### Users (Admin Screen)

The Admin screen (`app/admin.tsx`) displays registered users based on the `User` interface. This data is expected to come from the Airtable Attendees table (`tblQhLaWbOSI0t7iX`), potentially combined with authentication system data.

**Frontend Interface (`app/admin.tsx`):**

```typescript
interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  company: string | null;
  title: string | null;
  phone: string | null;
  image: string | null;
  bio: string | null;
  emailVerified: boolean | null;
  role: string;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

**Expected Airtable Field Mappings (from initial prompt and interface):**

*   **`id`**: Airtable record ID.
*   **`email`**: User's email address.
*   **`name`**: User's full name.
*   **`company`**: User's company.
*   **`title`**: User's job title.
*   **`phone`**: User's phone number.
*   **`image`**: URL of the user's photo (likely from an attachment field).
*   **`bio`**: User's biography.
*   **`emailVerified`**: Status of email verification (likely from the authentication system).
*   **`role`**: User's role (e.g., "admin", "attendee").
*   **`createdAt`**: Timestamp when the user registered.
